r Universitaire Vaudois (CHUV), Chemin des Falaises 1, Lausanne, 1011, Switzerland</aff><aff id="aff2"><label>2</label>Unit&#x000e9; d&#x02019;&#x000e9;pid&#x000e9;miologie du cancer, Institut universitaire de m&#x000e9;decine sociale et pr&#x000e9;ventive, rue du Bugnon 17, Lausanne, 1005, Switzerland</aff><aff id="aff3"><label>3</label>Anatomia Patologica 2, Spedali Civili, Piazza Spedali Civili 1, Brescia, 25124, Italy</aff><aff id="aff4"><label>4</label>Istituto di Ricerche Farmacologiche &#x02018;Mario Negri&#x02019;, Via Eritrea 62, Milano, 20157, Italy</aff><aff id="aff5"><label>5</label>Istituto di Statistica Medica e Biometria, Universit&#x000e0; degli Studi di Milano, Via Venezian 1, Milano, 20133, Italy</aff><pub-date pub-type="epub"><day>04</day><month>09</month><year>2000</year></pub-date><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><month>10</month><year>2000</year></pub-date><volume>83</volume><issue>7</issue><fpage>952</fpage><lpage>955</lpage><history><date date-type="received"><day>18</day><month>05</month><year>2000</year></date><date date-type="rev-recd"><day>15</day><month>06</month><year>2000</year></date><date date-type="accepted"><day>15</day><month>06</month><year>2000</year></date></history><copyright-statement>Copyright 2000, Cancer Research Campaign</copyright-statement><copyright-year>2000</copyright-year><permissions><copyright-holder>Cancer Research Campaign</copyright-holder></permissions><abstract><p>In Vaud, Switzerland, the incidence of carcinoids based on 218 malignant and 215 benign cases rose from 19.6/10<sup>6</sup>in 1974&#x02013;85 to 28.2/10<sup>6</sup>in 1986&#x02013;97, more so among males and malignant neoplasms. Lung was the commonest site for malignant and large intestine for benign carcinoids. Sixty-eight (16&#x00025;) carcinoids had another neoplasm. &#x000a9; 2000 Cancer Research Campaign</p></abstract><kwd-group><kwd>carcinoid</kwd><kwd>epidemiology</kwd><kwd>incidence</kwd><kwd>registry</kwd><kwd>time trends</kwd><kwd>survival</kwd><kwd>intestinal</kwd><kwd>lung</kwd><kwd>second primary tumour</kwd></kwd-group></article-meta></front></article>